Package: rbloo
Title: Rao-Blackwellised Leave-One-Out for Hierarchical Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Aidan", "D. Bindoff", email = "aidan.bindoff@utas.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0943-2702"))
Description: A closed-form, a-priori triage-and-cure for hierarchical
    cross-validation. The Gelman-Pardoe pooling factor and structural leverage
    (the fibr package) predict, before any importance weights are formed, which
    PSIS-LOO folds will be unreliable. Rao-Blackwellised LOO then marginalises
    the random-effect block -- analytically for the Gaussian case, by cheap 1-D
    quadrature for Bernoulli, binomial and Poisson GLMMs -- so the fiber-driven
    failures disappear at zero refit cost, matching exact refits. Residual folds
    are flagged for a genuine refit. Compatible with 'brms', 'rstanarm' and
    'smoothbp' fits and the 'loo' ecosystem.
